  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Some behind the screens scripting magic so when user gets the  edge of the current experience they go through some kind of fog or forest or portal showing the next experience dimly in the distance and end up in next world [which is loading in the background of course]. \n\nThis was one of the biggest strengths of Second Life in my opinion, the looking out across different regions and then being able to walk/fly there, as well as being able to directly enter any map you had a link for. \n\nOf course this is probably hard or will create tons of problems and from only the user perspective it would be great! No more loading screen in space! I stay immersed and exploring the whole time and can take my crew with me!",
